// =====================================================================================
// D3 - Workload identity multi-resource burst sign-in (lateral movement)
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Maps to  : POC Test D - Multi-Resource Burst Sign-In
// Table    : AADServicePrincipalSignInLogs  (diagnostic category: ServicePrincipalSignInLogs)
// Severity : 2 (Warning)
// MITRE    : T1078 (Valid Accounts) + T1087 (Account Discovery)
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What it finds
//   A single service principal that authenticated to an unusual number of DISTINCT
//   resources inside a 10 minute window - Graph, ARM, Key Vault, Storage, SQL, Power BI,
//   Fabric, and so on.
//
// Why it matters
//   A legitimate workload identity is provisioned for a job and touches one or two
//   resources forever. An attacker holding a stolen credential does not know what it can
//   reach, so they enumerate. The shape of that enumeration - many resources, seconds
//   apart, from one identity - is what this catches. No agent or sensor required; it is
//   pure token issuance telemetry, so it is invisible to the attacker.
//
// Tuning
//   ResourceThreshold is the only knob. Start at 4. Raise it if you run legitimate
//   orchestrators (backup, CSPM scanners, cost tools) that legitimately fan out; better
//   still, exclude those AppIds explicitly with the KnownFanOutApps line below.
//
// Triage
//   1. Do the resources form a coherent job, or do they look like a shopping list?
//   2. Same source IP for all of them, or spread?
//   3. Cross-check the AppId against D1 - a burst shortly after a credential addition
//      is the classic compromise sequence.
// =====================================================================================

let Lookback = 24h;
let BurstWindow = 10m;
let ResourceThreshold = 4;
// Add the AppIds of sanctioned fan-out identities here to suppress known-good noise.
let KnownFanOutApps = dynamic([]);
AADServicePrincipalSignInLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(Lookback)
| where ResultType == 0
| where AppId !in (KnownFanOutApps)
| summarize
    DistinctResources = dcount(ResourceDisplayName),
    Resources         = make_set(ResourceDisplayName, 20),
    SignIns           = count(),
    FirstSeen         = min(TimeGenerated),
    LastSeen          = max(TimeGenerated),
    SourceIPs         = make_set(IPAddress, 10)
    by ServicePrincipalName, ServicePrincipalId, AppId, BurstBin = bin(TimeGenerated, BurstWindow)
| where DistinctResources >= ResourceThreshold
| extend BurstDurationSeconds = datetime_diff('second', LastSeen, FirstSeen)
| order by DistinctResources desc, BurstDurationSeconds asc
